Чтобы создать бота Discord с одной командой бан, используйте следующие шаги:

1. Сначала, установите Discord.js v14 и другие зависимости, если вы этого еще не сделали:

   ```
   npm install discord.js @discordjs/rest discord.js-commando
   ```

2. Создайте файл `config.json` и вставьте в него следующие настройки:

   ```json
   {
     "token": "YOUR_DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN",
     "clientID": "YOUR_CLIENT_ID",
     "guildID": "YOUR_GUILD_ID"
   }
   ```

   - `YOUR_DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN`: Вставьте токен вашего Discord бота в эту строку.
   - `YOUR_CLIENT_ID`: Вставьте ID клиента вашего Discord бота в эту строку.
   - `YOUR_GUILD_ID`: Вставьте ID сервера Discord, на котором будет работать ваш бот в эту строку.

3. Создайте новый файл `index.js` и вставьте в него следующий код:

   ```javascript
   const { Client, GatewayIntentBits } = require("discord.js");
   const { REST } = require("@discordjs/rest");

   const fs = require("fs");

   const { clientId, guildId, token } = require("./config.json");

   const commands = [];
   const commandFiles = fs.readdirSync("./commands").filter(file => file.endsWith(".js"));

   for (const file of commandFiles) {
     const command = require(`./commands/${file}`);
     commands.push(command.data);
   }

   const rest = new REST({ version: "14" }).setToken(token);

   async function registerCommands() {
     try {
       if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== "production") {
         await rest.put(
           `https://discord.com/api/v${process.env.VITE_DISCORDJS_VERSION}/guilds/${guildId}/commands`,
           { body: commands }
         );
       } else {
         await rest.put(
           `https://discord.com/api/v${process.env.VITE_DISCORDJS_VERSION}/apps/${clientId}/guilds/${guildId}/commands`,
           { body: commands }
         );
       }
       console.log("Successfully registered application commands.");
     } catch (error) {
       console.error(error);
     }
   }

   async function main() {
     const client = new Client({
       intents: [
         GatewayIntentBits.Guilds,
         GatewayIntentBits.GuildMessages,
         GatewayIntentBits.MessageContent,
       ],
     });

     client.on("ready", () => {
       console.log("Bot is ready!");
     });

     client.on("interactionCreate", async interaction => {
       if (!interaction.isChatInputCommand()) return;

       const command = commands.find(c => c.name === interaction.commandName);

       try {
         await command.execute(interaction);
       } catch (error) {
         console.error(error);
         await interaction.reply({ content: "There was an error while executing this command!", ephemeral: true });
       }
     });

     await registerCommands();

     client.login(token);
   }

   main();
   ```

   - В данном примере, мы используем `Commando` библиотеку, поэтому нам нужен `commando.js`. Если вы хотите использовать другие библиотеки, необходимо изменить код в соответствии с вашей библиотекой.

4. Создайте новый файл `commandBan.js` в папке `./commands` и вставьте в него следующий код:

   ```javascript
   const { SlashCommandBuilder } = require("@discordjs/builders");

   module.exports = {
     data: new SlashCommandBuilder()
       .setName("ban")
       .setDescription("Bans the specified user from the server.")
       .addUserOption(option =>
         option.setName("user")
           .setDescription("The user to ban.")
           .setRequired(true)),
     async execute(interaction) {
       const user = interaction.options.getUser("user");

       await interaction.guild.members.ban(user, { days: 7, reason: "Banned by command" });

       await interaction.reply(`Successfully banned ${user.tag}`);
     },
   };
   ```

   - Замените `7` на число дней, на которое вы хотите банить пользователя.

5. В файле `package.json`, добавьте следующую секцию:

   ```json
   "scripts": {
     "start": "node index.js"
   },
   ```

6. Выполните команду `npm start` в консоли, чтобы запустить бота.

С этим кодом, ваш бот сможет использовать команду бан в вашем Discord сервере. Обратите внимание, что вам необходимо создать и настроить канал логирования, чтобы отслеживать ошибки и другие события, связанные с вашим ботом.

To create a high-quality testing environment in Cypress with Docker, and enable Cypress to take screenshots and save them, follow these steps:

1. Install and set up Docker on your local machine.

2. Create a new Cypress project using the Cypress CLI:

   ```
   npx cypress create my-project
   ```

3. Navigate to your Cypress project directory:

   ```
   cd my-project
   ```

4. In the root of your Cypress project, create a new file named `Dockerfile` (without an extension).

5. Add the following content to your `Dockerfile`:

   ```
   FROM node:14

   WORKDIR /app

   COPY package*.json ./

   RUN npm install

   COPY . .

   CMD ["npm", "run", "test"]
   ```

6. Create a new file named `package.json` in the root of your Cypress project:

   ```
   {
     "scripts": {
       "test": "cypress run"
     }
   }
   ```

7. Add Cypress dependencies to your `package.json` file:

   ```
   {
     "name": "my-project",
     "version": "1.0.0",
     "description": "",
     "main": "index.js",
     "scripts": {
       "test": "cypress run"
     },
     "keywords": [],
     "author": "",
     "license": "ISC",
     "dependencies": {
       "cypress": "^6.9.1",
       "cypress-docker-plugins": "^2.0.1",
       "cypress-multi-reporters": "^1.2.6",
       "cypress-xpath": "^3.0.0"
     },
     "devDependencies": {}
   }
   ```

8. Install Cypress dependencies using npm:

   ```
   npm install
   ```

9. Add the following Cypress plugins to your `cypress/plugins/index.js` file:

   ```
   const { addPlugin } = require("cypress/multi-reporters/plugins");

   module.exports = (on, config) => {
     on("file:preprocessor", (file, its) => {
       its.content = its.readAssets(file.path).content;
     });

     addPlugin(require("cypress-docker-plugins/plugin"));
   };
   ```

10. Add the following Cypress configuration to your `cypress.json` file:

   ```
   {
     "baseUrl": "http://localhost:8080",
     "reporterEnabled": "mochawesome",
     "reporterOptions": {
       "reportDir": "cypress/reports",
       "overwrite": false,
       "json": true,
       "html": true,
       "cliReport": false
     },
     "experimentalInteractiveRun": true,
     "chromeWebSecurity": false,
     "pluginsFile": "cypress/plugins/index.js",
     "screenshotOnRunFailure": true,
     "viewportPreferred": "macbook-13-inch",
     "viewportPresets": ["macbook-13-inch"],
     "video": false,
     "fixturesFolder": "cypress/fixtures",
     "integrationFolder": "cypress/integration",
     "supportFile": "cypress/support/commands.js",
     "pageLoadTimeout": 60000,
     "responseTimeout": 30000,
     "watchForFileChanges": true
   }
   ```

11. Create a new directory named `cypress` in the root of your project.

12. Inside the `cypress` directory, create a new directory named `fixtures`.

13. Inside the `cypress` directory, create a new directory named `integration`.

14. Inside the `cypress` directory, create a new file named `commands.js` in the `support` directory.

15. In the `commands.js` file, add the following content:

   ```
   import { addMethod } from "cypress-xpath";

   addMethod("containsXpath", (subject, xpath) => {
     const $el = Cypress.$(subject);
     return $el.filter(function() {
       return this.matches(xpath);
     });
   });

   Cypress.Commands.add("getByXpath", { prevSubject: true }, (subject, xpath) => {
     return subject.containsXpath(xpath).should("be.visible");
   });
   ```

16. Create a new directory named `screenshots` in the root of your project.

17. Add the following content to your `cypress.config.js` file:

   ```
   const { defineConfig } = require("cypress");

   module.exports = defineConfig({
     video: false,
     screenshotOnRunFailure: true,
     screenshotFolder: "cypress/screenshots",
     videoUploadOnPasses: false,
     videoUploadOnFailures: true,
     viewportWidth: 1280,
     viewportHeight: 720,
   });
   ```

18. Build your Docker image:

   ```
   docker build -t my-cypress-project .
   ```

19. Start your Cypress test runner using Docker:

   ```
   docker run -e CYPRESS_baseUrl=http://localhost:8080 -v $(pwd):/app my-cypress-project
   ```

20. Run your Cypress tests:

   ```
   docker run -e CYPRESS_baseUrl=http://localhost:8080 -v $(pwd):/app my-cypress-project cypress run
   ```

   This will run your Cypress tests, taking screenshots on failures and saving them to the `screenshots` directory in your project.

21. To take screenshots on test passes, update your `cypress.config.js` file:

   ```
   const { defineConfig } = require("cypress");

   module.exports = defineConfig({
     video: false,
     screenshotOnRunFailure: true,
     screenshotFolder: "cypress/screenshots",
     videoUploadOnPasses: true,
     videoUploadOnFailures: true,
     viewportWidth: 1280,
     viewportHeight: 720,
   });
   ```

   This will enable screenshots on both test failures and passes.

